>> title: Shichimi Togarashi
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: japanese, chiles, sesame, spice blend, pantry
>> servings: 16
>> time: 20 min
>> step.1: toast in a dry skillet 3 min
>> step.2: grind coarse in a mortar
>> step.3: stir in
>> step.4: fold in

Toast @black sesame seeds{2%Tbs}, @poppy seeds{1%Tbs}, and @hemp seeds{1%Tbs} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat until they smell nutty and start to pop, about ~{3%min}.

Grind @dried mandarin peel{1%Tbs} and @toasted nori{1%sheet}(torn small) to a coarse powder in a #mortar{}.

Stir @&(~1)peel powder{} into @&(~2)toasted seeds{}.

Fold @ground dried chile{3%Tbs}(ichimi togarashi) and @ground sansho pepper{1%tsp} into @&(~1)mixture{}.
